From e9a806d56f88f63efded8ec14f8487afbc863b0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JuggyMcNutty <11588877+JuggyMcNutty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 16:55:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Collision: moves and traces without casts or allocations

FORK ONLY. This project ships a NO-AI Code Rule asking that LLM-written
changes stay in a fork and are never PR'd upstream. These were written with
Claude. Do not submit them.

Around the geometry of every move and trace:

- TraceMove and FinishMove asked with two dynamic_casts whether the mover
  is a UPlayerPawn or a UProjectile (which block and are blocked by
  bBlockPlayers), and again for every actor the move met. An object's C++
  class never changes: UActor::IsPlayerOrProjectile makes the casts once
  and keeps the answer.
- Every trace sorted its hits with std::stable_sort, which takes a buffer
  from the heap each time, twice for a trace that reaches the world. A
  trace's hits are few: CollisionHitList::SortByFraction is an insertion
  sort, which leaves them in the order std::stable_sort did.
- TraceTester::Trace kept the first hit for each actor with a std::set,
  one allocation per actor hit; the hits kept are few, so it scans them.

Checked with the frame time and random seeds temporarily fixed: a hash of
every actor's location, rotation, velocity, state and class matched the
build before patch 0028, frame by frame, on Liberty Island and UNATCO HQ.
